WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.800
Shadow, wood, sword, thunder, power, sleep

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.760
Cardcaptors of the Clow expect the unexpected now

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.140
The secrets of the Clow were all a mystery

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.510
But when this mighty book was opened

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.510
The powers were set free

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.670
Cardcaptors, a mystic adventure

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.710
Cardcaptors, a quest for all time

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.630
Each card possesses a power on its own

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.970
You've got to find them to bring the power home

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.870
THE CLOUD IN CHE-

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:04.640
That just...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.040
Out of it!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:33.060
Huh?

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.980
No doubt you have a perfectly logical explanation for that.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:44.880
Sorry!

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:46.810
What's going on?

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:48.350
Yeah...

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:58.260
Well, you know, Kira, I keep having that same dream about this kid on a tower with the cloud cards.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:58.600
Huh?

00:01:58.820 --> 00:01:59.100
Fine!

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.390
Hmm. Sounds like you got company.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.240
Is that right?

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.820
Well, whatever you say, Squirt. I heard voices.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.300
Nobody's in here.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.430
Everybody knows stuff toys can't talk, Tori.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:21.840
Mm-hmm.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.710
I think you're really losing it, Squirt.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:27.030
Yeah!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.740
Oh, by the way, I'm leaving in tents, so...

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:52.820
Get over it, Sakura.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.590
That big a fist to fry, kiddo.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.440
For example...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.340
What?

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.220
Capturing the cloud cards?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.420
Yeah, I know that.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.260
But do you really, Sakura?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.380
Look, kid, you gotta expect things.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.300
When you least expect them.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:09.620
Huh?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.870
Sakura, you're going to be late.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.850
Get easy.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.220
That's what happens when you sit in your room talking to yourself.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.320
Tori, I was not.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.960
Hey, Julian.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.260
Uh, hi.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:46.780
Sorry we're late.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.820
The squirt was having a very deep conversation.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.530
Giving you a hard time again?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.330
I know what I heard.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.970
She's ten years old.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.190
and still talks to imaginary friends.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.290
It's pretty pathetic, don't you think?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.110
Are you feeling okay?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.410
Oh, yeah.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.190
I had a strange dream last night.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.050
Yeah?

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.770
Dreams can tell you what you least expect.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:16.200
Huh?

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:17.500
The unexpected.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.540
That's just what Kiro said.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.970
In fact, this morning I had a dream just like that.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:25.450
Yeah?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.330
Very déjà vu.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.130
It was really quite amazing.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:29.970
I dreamt that I...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.540
I'd have French toast for breakfast.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.380
And you know what?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.100
I did.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:34.920
Whoa.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.360
Another video camera.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.590
It's a new digital version my mom got.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:42.170
Great.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:46.170
And sorry, but chrominance reduction is a good thing.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.970
It cuts down the color noise.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:49.950
And we are noisy.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.240
Hey, guys.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.390
Morning, Rita.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:55.540
Go in.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.020
Good morning, class.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.360
Take your seats, please.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:17.950
Hmm. Hope you all had a good weekend. I have a surprise for you. We have a new exchange student, Lee Shoron. Come on in.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.840
Why do you suppose we're getting an exchange student this time of year? I don't know.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.980
Welcome, Lee, to Readington Elementary.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.640
Okay, Lee, where should we seat you?

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:57.660
Let's see now.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.780
Why don't you sit behind...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:12.570
There are seats over here.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.440
Lee?

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:15.050
Hi.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.390
What does he want from me?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:47.660
Excuse me?

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:48.670
What?

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.510
Force of light with ancient spin

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.190
Send forth the magic power within

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:59.930
Oracles of gold, wood, water, fire

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.940
rain and electricity

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.630
or snow my plight

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.090
I know you've got them.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.520
Even if I did, I'm not giving them to you.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:41.340
I'm capturing them for Kiro.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:42.850
Wait a minute.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.160
Do you mean Kiro Barros?

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.600
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.820
Since when does a Guardian Beast let someone like you handle the Cloud Cards?

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:56.080
Accidentally let the cards out of the Cloud Book.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.760
I didn't even know what it was.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:58.720
So where do you?

00:07:58.800 --> 00:07:58.940
Ha!

00:07:59.390 --> 00:07:59.970
Kiro Barros!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.200
was supposed to guard the cloud cards.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.810
Don't tell me they all escaped.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:06.940
Yep.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.450
But you got some of them back, right?

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.200
Yeah, a few.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.020
I'm working on it.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.890
And you're a card captor?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.390
That's pretty pathetic.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.510
So I hear.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:20.910
Wait!

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:24.250
How do you know about the cloud cards anyway?

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.730
That's none of your business.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.680
But I'm taking over.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.700
Give them to me!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.530
Exactly. Who do you think you are, Wei Li?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.890
You'd be surprised. Give me the cards.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:10.040
Don't pick on my sister, kid. Why don't you go home before someone gets hurt? Namely you.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.960
So what did you think of the physics exam? Sure good thing we reviewed quasars, huh?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.680
Oh, uh, hi.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:34.360
There's lots.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.020
One for you, one for you, and one for you.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.200
Here.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.020
You want some?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.560
Guess he's not hungry.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.200
Kiro will know what to do about that Lee guy?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.000
Sure. He's the guardian of the cloud cards.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:10.320
Right. He's probably at home right now, planning our next move.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.360
Yeah, I bet you're right.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:22.990
See you today.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:33.650
He tried to take the cloud cards. Well...

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.710
Expect the unexpected, Sakura.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:36.790
That's it?

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.430
Don't forget, you are a cardcaptor now.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.760
You know, you've been chosen to get the cloud cards back.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.760
And that's what you gotta be worried about.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.780
Not some insignificant little schoolyard scuffle.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:48.300
What?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.930
This is powerful magic we're dealing with here.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:53.160
Uh-huh.

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.420
There are gonna be a few bumps along the way.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.970
Kiro, he tried to take the cloud...

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.220
Maybe it's time for a little history lesson.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.020
Sorcery is an ancient tradition.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.800
Now, most sorcerers practice in line with their traditions.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:15.700
But my master, Clow Reed, created a new kind of magic when he created the Clow Cards.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.100
Great, but what's that got to do with Lee Sho Ron?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:21.900
Yeah, I'm getting to that part.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:22.840
What do you mean, Kiro?

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.220
Huh? There are some people who study magic all of their lives.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.980
Well, you can see that they're, uh, born...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:41.140
into the tradition. Your point is? Lee Shoran is a descendant of Clow Reed. What? Lee's part of

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:48.320
Clow Reed's family. I should have given him these cards after all. Doesn't work like that. Why? Sakura,

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:56.410
try and keep up, will ya? The cards were in the book. The book had a seal on it. You broke the seal.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.790
And only person with specially chosen

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.540
powers has that kind of ability. Don't you get it? You're the one who found the book,

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:15.100
the one who signed the cards. You have the right to them. You're the one who's destined

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:28.640
to have them. Sakura speaking. Sakura. Oh, hey, Madison. Gotta look outside.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:31.050
Why?

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.910
You've got some cards picture.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:36.650
Wow, I guess I do.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:39.340
I'll meet you in ten.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.580
Now you're talking.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.840
Pink frills, Madison?

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.000
It's not pink, it's Cyber Rose.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.460
It's high-tech and it's in all the magazines, Sakura.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.480
Huh? High-tech, huh?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:55.060
Non-conducting titanium and rubber.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.600
Well, uh, she's got a point there.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.560
Rubber will protect you from lightning.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.310
Only for you, Madison.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:15.830
You're going to thank me?

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:28.620
Some kind of magic device with him?

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:29.980
Uh-huh. He called...

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:36.110
That gives him a predictive edge that could be a little problematic for us.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.190
Don't worry, you're the rifle card captor.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.850
We'll just capture that Thunder Card before the lead kid manages to show up.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.390
That's right, I'll show him.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.750
Transform it to its visible form.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.330
And that would be how?

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:02.110
Heads up!

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:02.390
Huh?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.400
Force, know my plight! Release the light!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.460
I'm looking at Raiju, the Thunderbeast.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:10.960
Boy, you are hopeless.

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:11.860
Back off.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:14.640
Listen up, Lee. She is just getting stunned.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.060
The Windy Card will take care of this.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:23.230
Put it away. Windy can't stand up against Thunder.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.590
But, Lee, I've captured other cards using the Windy Card.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.980
In case you hadn't...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.720
Notice, kids, your Raizu remains on the warpath while you keep arguing.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.030
Shadow card, don't you?

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:43.750
Uh-huh.

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:44.250
Okay.

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.930
Force, Nomide Blight. Release the light.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.130
Lightning!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.340
Boy, you really don't have a clue about this, do you?

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:47.830
Hey, hey, Daisy! Everybody's got to start somewhere.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:50.230
Huh? What's this thing?

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:51.780
This is Kira!

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:57.670
No way! Kira Barrows? The Guardian Beast of the Seal?

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.970
The greatest Guardian Beast of all...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.340
The beast with the golden eyes

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:04.040
Is a stuffed animal

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:15.270
You are a joke

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:18.880
I was appointed by Clow Reed himself

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.260
A lot of good that did

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.080
Hi, Lee

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.230
Whatever

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:28.670
Chrome and introduction were great

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:33.680
Hey, you pulled it off.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:39.010
But this is only the beginning.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:53.550
Just between you and Mitch, good idea, huh?

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.100
Kura's battle costume.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.200
Pretty wild, don't you think?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:07.140
Madison made this battle outfit with an apron over the top, a tail like a cat, and bells, too.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:10.240
She called it very in, but high-tech, too, remember?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:16.420
Now, see, Sakura was battling against thunder, so Madison had to make it out of materials that wouldn't conduct electricity.

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:19.820
And now, check out this!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.580
Rear gun protection. That great big bow is non-conducting, too.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:25.460
Now, the ears, well, they're just for decoration.

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.280
Madison may be a techno nut, but, you know, she just couldn't resist.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:29.980
And that's how...

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:37.050
I guarantee that Madison has got a zillion ideas for even wilder battle costumes in the episodes to come.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:38.170
So stay tuned.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:39.190
See ya.
